  "reason": "The abstract discusses the use of New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) in chemical risk assessment, including in silico, in chemico, and in vitro assays. While it mentions case studies to build confidence in their usability and explore their domains of applicability, it does not report any quantitative measure of agreement between non-human animal results and human clinical results. The focus is on improving risk assessment and regulatory decision-making using NAMs, rather than comparing the predictive accuracy of animal models to human outcomes."
